# [[.BinaryName]]

[[.Description]]

A [zhi](https://github.com/MrWong99/zhi) **[[.PluginType]]** plugin.

## Building

```bash
# Build for the current platform
make build

# Cross-compile for all supported platforms
make cross-compile

# Run tests
make test

# Run all checks (format, vet, lint, test)
make check
```

## Development

The plugin implementation is in `pkg/plugin/plugin.go`. A sample workspace
is provided in `workspace/` so you can test your plugin locally:

```bash
# Build the plugin
make build

# Run the workspace (requires zhi CLI)
cd workspace
zhi list
zhi validate
```

## Publishing

Build cross-platform binaries and publish to an OCI registry:

```bash
make cross-compile
zhi plugin publish --registry [[if .Registry]][[.Registry]][[else]]ghcr.io/<your-org>[[end]]
```

Or push a version tag to trigger the GitHub Actions release workflow.

